            "review_title": "Review at Green Pepper Beer Corner",
            "review_text": "mikeethegerman\nColorado23 contributions\n0\nRestaurant is irrelevant\nFeb 2017 • Solo\nDoes not matter where you are on beer corner, but you have to be on the CORNER, not down tourist street, and you will experience the most amazing production nobody ever staged.\n\nBetween twice a night raids by the police for having chairs too far in traffic you have your Viet beauties in short skirts and moderate heels handing out cigarattes, mom and dad and 2 kids on motor scooter headed home, a guy in in his 500 Mercedes trying to impress the ladies, the 67 year old hippie from the Vietnam war, along with the 19 year old nursing student from Singapore. Drop all this humanity in a mixer, add 17 motorcycles and 12 moving violations, in 10 seconds and you have an idea what beer corner is like for the time it takes to read this. And the next 10 second segment will probably be different involving, tourists, locals, cars, cops, neon, inflated pigs and garbage trucks playing Viet folk music. \n\nGot too many beers? Missed dinner? Flying food vendors will sell you great food right at your chair. \n\nAnd, yes the beers (at least reputable brands) are now up to 20,000 dong, or roughly 85 cents per 18 ounce bottle.\n\nGOOOOD Night Vietnam!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 28, 2017",
